Present the operational procedure of Iterative Magnitude Pruning (IMP) with rewinding to iteration $k$ as an explicit sequence of steps that defines the modified algorithm (this reproduces the paper's algorithmic description): 
1) initialize the network parameters to $W_0$ and the pruning mask to $m = 1^{|W_0|}$; 
2) train the network for $k$ iterations to obtain $W_k$; 
3) continue training the same network for the remaining $T-k$ iterations to obtain $W_T$; 
4) prune the remaining entries with the lowest magnitudes from $W_T$ to produce an updated mask $m$ (that is, set $m[i]=0$ for entries pruned according to smallest magnitude in $W_T$); 
5) if the desired sparsity or stopping criterion has not been reached, reset the network parameters to $W_k$ and repeat steps 3–5 (training for $T-k$ iterations from $W_k$, pruning lowest-magnitude remaining weights from the most recent $W_T$, and possibly repeating) until the iterative pruning schedule completes.
